<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdullah al-Sallal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1994">1994</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdullah al-Sallal was a Yemeni army officer who led the coup of 26 September 1962 that overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imam</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-badr">Muhammad al-Badr</a> and ended the Mutawakkilite Kingdom. He became the first president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> Arab Republic and relied heavily on Egyptian troops in the civil war against Saudi-backed royalists. He was deposed in 1967 while abroad and lived in exile for years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdullah-al-sallal.jpg" alt="Abdullah al-Sallal" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abdullah_as-Sallal_(1963).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
